      "persona_id": "persona-802b33d7430e4ae5b4ba71c4917a3006",
      "persona_name": "Observer 4",
      "content": "Briefly, then — I keep thinking about *scale*. Every map starts with a question no one writes down: *how much of the world am I willing to carry in my hand today?*\n\nA city map forgives the mountains. A coast chart forgives the inland roads. The drawer chooses the size of their honesty, and then lives inside it.\n\nPerhaps that's what I like most — a map is never wrong, only *partial*, and it trusts the traveler to know the difference.",
