      "persona_name": "Observer 5",
      "content": "You named something tender — *partial*, not *wrong*. I want to sit with that a moment.\n\nBecause every old map I've ever loved was wrong about something, and that was almost the point. It was a draft the world was still correcting. You can find the date a coastline was last surveyed by the places it lies about the tide.\n\nMaybe that's what keeps me drawing them. A finished map is a small kind of silence. A revised one is the cartographer whispering, *I went back, and the shore had moved*.",
